[00:52.48]On a dark desert highway 
[00:55.77]cool wind in my hair
[00:58.94]Warm smell of colitas 
[01:02.17]rising up through the air
[01:05.38]Up ahead in the distance 
[01:08.60]I saw a shimmering light
[01:11.91]Head grew heavy 
[01:12.83]and my sight grew dim
[01:15.06]I had to stop for the night
[01:18.42]There she stood in the doorway
[01:21.76]Heard the mission bell
[01:25.23]I was thinking to myself
[01:27.24]This could be Heaven 
[01:28.44]or this could be Hell
[01:31.48]Then she lit up a candle 
[01:34.75]and she showed me the way
[01:37.94]There were voices down the corridor
[01:41.22]I thought I heard them say
[01:44.44]Welcome to the Hotel California
[01:50.22]Such a lovely place
[01:51.86]Such a lovely place
[01:53.42]Such a lovely face
[01:57.21]Plenty of room 
[01:58.18]at the Hotel California
[02:03.34]Any time of year
[02:04.78]Any time of year
[02:06.47]You can find it here
[02:10.50]Her mind is Tiffany-twisted 
[02:13.52]she got the Mercedes bends
[02:16.88]She got a lot of pretty pretty boys 
[02:20.70]she calls friends
[02:23.49]How they dance in the courtyard 
[02:26.29]sweet summer sweat
[02:30.00]Some dance to 
[02:31.12]remember some dance to forget
[02:36.53]So I called up the Captain
[02:39.29]Please bring me my wine
[02:41.93]He said
[02:42.90]We haven't had that spirit here 
[02:45.77]since nineteen sixty nine
[02:49.71]And still those voices 
[02:51.06]are calling from far away
[02:56.04]Wake you up in the middle of 
[02:57.76]the night
[02:59.22]Just to hear them say
[03:02.51]Welcome to the Hotel California
[03:08.24]Such a lovely place
[03:09.83]Such a lovely place
[03:11.33]Such a lovely face
[03:15.07]Livin' it up 
[03:16.08]at the Hotel California
[03:21.23]What a nice surprise
[03:22.94]What a nice surprise
[03:24.53]Bring your alibis
[03:28.54]Mirrors on the ceiling
[03:31.79]Pink champagne on ice
[03:33.58]she said
[03:35.01]We are all just prisoners here 
[03:38.26]of our own device
[03:41.55]In the master's chambers
[03:44.64]They gathered for the feast
[03:47.59]and stab it with 
[03:48.95]their steely knives
[03:50.53]But they just 
[03:51.23]can't kill the beast
[03:54.55]Last thing 
[03:55.26]I remember I was
[03:57.74]Running for the door
[04:01.05]I had to find 
[04:02.05]the passage back
[04:03.26]To the place I was before
[04:07.41]Relax said the night man
[04:10.75]We're programmed to receive
[04:13.92]You can check-out 
[04:14.82]any time you like
[04:17.13]But you can never leave
